1. What is a fuzzy set?
A fuzzy set is a set in which elements have membership values between 0 and 1.
2. What is a membership value?
It represents how strongly an element belongs to a fuzzy set.
3. What is fuzzy union?
It selects the maximum membership value from two fuzzy sets.
4. What is fuzzy intersection?
It selects the minimum membership value from two fuzzy sets.
5. What is the complement of a fuzzy set?
It is calculated by subtracting each membership value from 1.
6. What is a Cartesian product in fuzzy logic?
It creates a fuzzy relation by taking the minimum membership value for every pair of elements.
7. What is max-min composition?
It is a method in which we first calculate minimum values and then select the maximum value.
8. Which library is used in this program?
NumPy is used for numerical calculations and matrix operations.
9. Is an external dataset required?
No. Fuzzy sets are directly defined in the program, so no external dataset is required.

